Count Subarrays with given XOR
Given an array of integers arr[] and a number k, count the number of subarrays having XOR of their elements as k.

Explanation:
THis is same as counting subarrays with sum k... instead of storing sum with prefix sum += nums[i]
we store prefixXor = prefixXor ^ nums[i]....

Otherwise all same

Code:
class Solution {
    public long subarrayXor(int arr[], int k) {
        // code here
        HashMap<Integer, Integer> map = new HashMap<>();
        int prefixXor=0; int count=0;
        map.put(0,1);
        for(int i=0;i<arr.length;i++){
            int num = arr[i];
            prefixXor = prefixXor ^ num;
            int complement = prefixXor ^ k;
            if(map.containsKey(complement)){
                count+=map.get(complement);
            }
            map.put(prefixXor, map.getOrDefault(prefixXor,0)+1);
            
        }
        return count;
    }
}
